	abstract = {The safety distance detection in hazardous chemical warehouses based on automatic inspection vehicles is a very promising technical solution. High quality datasets are essential for developing reliable autonomous driving algorithms, but there is a significant shortage of such data. This paper uses a low-cost, easily deployable monocular camera and incorporates a pose expansion algorithm for synthetic viewpoint rendering within Neural Radiance Fields to expand RGB images. Using structured light technology to generate depth images, the RGB image and depth image are calculated by depth backprojection formula to obtain three-dimensional point cloud. Combined with environmental parameters and relevant standards and regulations, a multimodal dataset for hazardous chemicals warehouses is constructed. The quality of the dataset is assessed using multiple indicators. Experimental results show that this generation framework is effective and the dataset is comprehensive and accurate, providing valuable insights and research for constructing new datasets in related fields. © 2024 IEEE.},
