	abstract = {High demands on manufacturers have left their shipping warehouses in havoc. Human error features a negative effect on safety, efficiency, and quality. Automated Guided Vehicle frameworks are broadly utilized for shipping material in manufacturing and warehousing applications. These frameworks offer numerous preferences over different sorts of material vehicles. Nonetheless, the arranging of those frameworks is complex gratitude to the interrelated decisions that must be made and subsequently the sizable measure of framework plan options that are accessible. This work aimed to set up a low-cost electrically operated Automated Guided Vehicle framework that can be utilized for material taking care of in little-scale ventures for which costly frameworks like forklifts are not gainful. These expenses are reduced with the introduction of an electrically operated Automated Guided Vehicle. A driverless, intelligent forklift uses an optical path to quickly and safely traverse a warehouse. Its capabilities are enhanced by the ability to send and receive tasks through Radio Frequency data communication. Computer-controlled and wheel-based, Automated Guided Vehicles are load carriers that travel along the floor of a facility without an onboard operator or driver. Their movement is directed by a combination of software and sensor-based guidance systems. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd 2024.},
