	abstract = {Integration of industrial informatics and software-defined vehicle optimization is revolutionizing logistics. This study discusses how this integration may improve logistics safety, sustainability, and efficiency. Logistics are the backbone of international companies; thus, they must run smoothly. Industrial informatics and optimization studies yielded new findings. This powerful technology combines advanced machine learning algorithms, data analytics, and real-time monitoring to change logistics. Data-driven decisions are the foundation of industrial informatics. This research determines the best data analytics methods for gas and labor savings. Real-time monitoring keeps logistical operations adaptive to changing circumstances, while predictive maintenance and energy-efficient driving boost system efficiency. Nearest Neighbor, Branch and Bound, Particle Swarm Optimization, Monte Carlo Simulation, and Genetic Algorithms reveal that the suggested technique is superior. This study shows the indicated approach's considerable effect. Its cheaper pricing, faster delivery, and lesser carbon emissions make it better than conventional solutions. Logistics operations are safer with the proposed method, which has a higher safety score and fewer accidents and incidents. The suggested method benefits from its flexibility, scalability, and adaptability, which are crucial in a fast-changing firm. Expense savings: Save $250,000 using the proposed technique. The new method results in a time savings of 15.79%. The suggested approach reduces carbon emissions by 3,000 kg (26.09%). The suggested method improves safety ratings by 10 - 11.36%. © 2024 IEEE.},
