	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105003216327&partnerID=40&md5=3d6f8f23d1d36579bac72c660f68af9d},
	affiliations = {University of Moratuwa, Department of Transport and Logistics Management, Moratuwa, Sri Lanka; Aalborg University, Department of Materials and Production, Aalborg, Nordjylland, Denmark; College of Engineering and Science, Melbourne, FL, United States},
	abstract = {Stock take refers to the process of physically verifying the amounts and conditions of all commodities present in the warehouse. Instead of conducting this task on an annual basis, it would be more effective to perform it frequently. Workers in a cold storage warehouse face hazards throughout the stock-taking process, such as being exposed to low temperatures and working in elevated areas with ladders and heavy gear while required to have mandatory rest stops while working under extreme temperatures. Hence, conducting stocktaking operations using UAVs (Unmanned Areial Vehicles) can effectively reduce these risks and enhance the operational effectiveness of the facility. Even though battery drain is higher with the extreme temperature, modern high-density batteries are capable of performing this task in cold warehouse. Furthermore, this system reduce the overall time taken for stocktaking process improving the accuracy of the inventory compared to traditional system. The objective of this study is to identify an effective approach for stocktaking in cold storage using UAVs and creating an energy efficient routing system for the selected UAV system. UAV with a UGV (Unmanned Ground Vehicles) selected as the UAV system due to its benefits of safety, range and easy navigation compared to other systems. Considering the factors affecting the energy usage of UAV, we created energy aware routing system which is 25.6% efficient compared to traditional system in our simulated scenario. Then we compared the time taken for perform the same task using single and two UAV systems. Two UAV system performed the same task using 42.8% less time compared to single UAV system which made it beneficial in large scale warehouse stocktaking operations. © 2024 Computers and Industrial Engineering. All rights reserved.},
