	affiliations = {Central South University, School of Automation, Changsha, Hunan, China},
	abstract = {In modern industrial warehouses, heterogeneous and flexible fleets of automated guided vehicles (AGVs) are widely used to improve transport efficiency. However, as their scale and limit of battery capacity increase, the complexity of dynamic scheduling also increases dramatically. The problem is to assign tasks and determine detailed paths to AGVs to keep the multi-AGV system running efficiently and sustainedly. In this context, a mixed-integer linear programming (MILP) model is formulated. A hierarchical planning method is used, which decomposes the integrated problem into two levels: the upper-level task-assignment problem and the lower-level path-planning problem. A hybrid discrete state transition algorithm (HDSTA) based on an elite solution set and the Tabu List method is proposed to solve the dynamic scheduling problem to minimize the sum of the costs of requests and the tardiness costs of conflicts for the overall system. The efficacy of our method is investigated by computational experiments using real-world data. © © 2023 Hu, He and Shen.},
