	affiliations = {Ltd, Wenzhou, Zhejiang, China},
	abstract = {Automated warehouse system is a system that can automatically store and take out materials without direct manual treatment. Compared with foreign developed countries, there is a big gap in the number and construction level of automated three-dimensional warehouses in China. This topic is mainly aimed at the design of automated warehouse system based on PID algorithm. This system can maintain daily information, and carry out corresponding inventory as needed, such as establishing, modifying and deleting information. The control strategy of motor speed of stacker in storage system is studied, and the PID control strategy is optimized by IPSO (improved particle swarm optimization) algorithm. Cosine adjustment is introduced into the inertia weight of traditional PSO algorithm, which improves the deficiency of traditional PSO algorithm that it is easy to fall into local optimal solution in the later stage. The simulation results show that the IPSO algorithm optimizes the PID control motor speed system, and the motor speed performance has been greatly improved compared with that before optimization. In this paper, IPSO algorithm has excellent anti-interference ability, so it gets the best PID tuning result, which is better than the standard PSO algorithm. © 2023 IEEE.},
