	doi = {10.1145/3543303.3543314},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85139878733&doi=10.1145%2F3543303.3543314&partnerID=40&md5=933a5fb2c3b7b5bc60fcdf8252d3908f},
	affiliations = {Chongqing University of Posts and Telecommunications, School of Advanced Manufacturing Engineering, Chongqing, Chongqing, China},
	abstract = {The contemporary society has put forward higher requirements for the logistics system with the development of industrial production automation, intelligence and information integration. Automatic guided vehicle (AGV) is a kind of mobile wheeled robot which can complete the specified transportation task after given path information and map information. In AGV scheduling, AGV path planning is an important part of AGV scheduling system. On the basis of the developed AGV, this study focuses on the path planning technology of AGV in warehousing logistics. The main research contents are as follows. The method of global map environment modeling was studied. After analyzing several commonly adopted environment modeling methods, the grid method which was most suitable for warehouse map modeling was adopted. Based on the raster map model, the path planning technology of AGV was studied, including single AGV path planning technology and multi-AGV path planning technology. In the research of single AGV path planning, we first studied the single AGV path planning technology, and finally chose a new swarm intelligence algorithm-slime mould algorithm. On the basis of single AGV path planning, we continued to study the multi-AGV path planning technology. Firstly, several types of conflicts in multi-AGV path planning were summarized. In order to solve the conflicts, a time window model algorithm was proposed to effectively avoid conflicts. Finally, the scheduling cooperation and path planning of multi-AGV were realized. © 2022 ACM.},
