	doi = {10.1109/ICCTEIE54047.2021.9650647},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85124071073&doi=10.1109%2FICCTEIE54047.2021.9650647&partnerID=40&md5=c1e7ca8ebcaed29337ac99c0f5d59089},
	affiliations = {Universitas Diponegoro, Department of Mathematics, Semarang, Central Java, Indonesia},
	abstract = {This paper was prepared to discuss the application of the Robust Model Predictive Control (RMPC) results in decision-making automation of an inventory system with uncertain demand. The problem solved in this research involved controlling the inventory level of a single product warehouse under demand uncertainty to decide the volume of the product to be automatically ordered from suppliers using a controller design. The solution involved modeling the inventory level which is the product volume (units) stored in the warehouse as an output value of a dynamical equation in a discrete-time linear state-space equation while the product volume ordered from the supplier was modeled as the output value. The demand parameter was reputed as the disturbance in the dynamical system with some known probability distribution function and RMPC was applied to calculate the optimal input. This was followed by computer-based simulations to simulate the inventory system. The results showed the RMPC was able to effectively generate an optimal decision and the inventory level was also achieved as expected. © 2021 IEEE.},
