	abstract = {With the rapid development of the logistics industry, the requirements, and standards for the identification of goods in warehouse logistics have become higher and higher. Therefore, it needs to continuously strengthen the automatic identification ability of goods in warehouse logistics to improve and perfect the logistics management system. In this paper, the radio frequency identification (RFID) system is taken as the main research object, an automatic identification model of goods in warehouse logistics based on RFID technology is established, and six hundred goods in warehouse logistics are selected to carry out corresponding label identification research through RFID system. The experimental results of related parameters such as the number of goods identified correctly, the number of goods identified incorrectly, the number of goods rejected to identify, the stability, etc. are obtained. The experimental conclusions that the RFID system has better performance and stability for the automatic identification of goods in the warehouse logistics compared with the traditional cargo identification system, and the experimental results are significant are drawn. This study provides a new route for the research on automatic identification management of goods in warehousing logistics. © 2020 by Begell House, Inc.},
