	abstract = {Warehouse storage spaces assignment to items method almost effect on all key characteristics of warehouse efficiency. Cube-per-order index defines as the ratio of required space for storing each item to the number of its retrieval and demand request. In order to introduce some new impressing parameters for items layout in class-based storage, we tried to present a new index rather than before to encompass mentioned cases. Our multi-objective optimization problem model develops an allocation and product layout model in a class-based storage which applies an automatic storage and retrieval system (AS/RS) with considering energy consumption optimization and energy sustainability. Also, with adding the second objective to our model, we minimized energy costs while allocating items to locations with the minimum movement priority in AS/RS. Related model will be developed through decreasing electricity in allocation, optimum movement and consequently with helping to energy sustainability and reaching to sustainable manufacturing. In summary, with introducing the proposed model, recognizing affecting factors on mentioned index, applying analytical hierarchy process and incorporating experts opinions, we create this new index and examine the consistency of matrix (which weights are acquired from it) to determine the weight of each upon impressing criteria in allocation. Next, we run our developed model using Lingo software and by applying five multi-objective optimization techniques. © 2018, Islamic Azad University (IAU).},
