	affiliations = {Gautam Buddha University, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Greater Noida, UP, India},
	abstract = {RFID (Radio Frequency Identification) is an automatic identification method consisting of several components such as RFID tags, tag readers, edge servers, middleware, and application software. Among these the three important components are RFID tag (also known as transponder), RFID reader (also known as transceiver or interrogator) and software for data processing. The tags contain Electronic Product Code (EPC) and the information related to the product like the name of the company, batch and year of manufacturing, price, etc [1]. The purpose of this paper, first, is to provide guidelines for a gear manufacturing industry for implementing the RFID technology at different stages of receiving, storing, manufacturing and delivery. And, second, is to develop a real-time management approach to enable the product or parts to reach to the company via different suppliers in shorter time by integrating the RFID technology to ERP software packages of the company and the ERP software packages of the suppliers. This paper emphasis on the quality management and wastage elimination on the basis of cost justification for implementing the RFID technology with respect to internal and external failure costs. RFID is an appropriate technology for profit generation, efficiency improvement, and productivity enhancement [2]. Proposing the product flow model for the warehouse and tool-crib department and replicating the proposed model for warehouse management and tool-crib management for the gear manufacturing company in India. This would provide the real-time tracking facility for tool management and stock keeping. As India is the country where lot of automation is not suppose very good for the company and the society too. So, we will start here from small changes. Firstly using the RFID technology in warehouse and tool-crib of the gear manufacturing company. Then look for the further improvement slowly. Like the automating the assembly line for the differential-gears assembly. As the RFID is based on the concept of Radio Frequency, it can be interfered with other radio transmissions, metals, liquids, etc. The degree of interference depends upon the frequency of the tag and the usage environment. So, during the selection of tags and reader all the required parameters should be considered thoroughly. Here the company is using the bar-coding system for record updating. So we can use the RFID technology with integrated bar-coding system for making changes in small steps. © © INDIACom-2013.},
